ability.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-09\nValid as Of: 2024-10-09\nVersion: 26753\n\n--- Record 2140 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.24.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      Telemetry Manager: Reduced CPU usage if there's a high amount of Istio resources in the cluster (#1264).      Traces and Metrics: Update to OTel Collector 0.109.0 (#1465).      Logs: Update to Fluent Bit 3.1.8 (#1459).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-25\nValid as Of: 2024-10-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 201 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configurations API - Avoid Retry When Using Inactive Knowledge Bases\nDescription: An internal retry logic used to be applied to requests which failed because the corresponding knowledge base was inactive, which led to long response times. This issue has been corrected.  A knowledge base can become inactive if a customer triggers a reload from the administration UI by specifying a valid-from date later than the valid-from date of the used knowledge base.  See Administration Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-27\nValid as Of: 2025-08-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 202 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration of SAP Asset Performance Management with SAP Cloud Transport Management\nDescription: You can now use SAP Cloud Transport Management to transport SAP Asset Performance management content.  See:   Supported Content Types  Integrating SAP Cloud Transport Management with Other SAP Cloud Solutions  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-26\nValid as Of: 2025-08-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 203 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Modifiable transport requests\nDescription: You can create transport requests that are initially empty. You can use them to add multiple files and test the deployment of the files. After successful testing, you can release the transport requests. As a result, they become available for import.  See:   Processing Modifiable Transport Requests  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-26\nValid as Of: 2025-08-26\nVersion: 2508a\n\n--- Record 204 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New ImportSelectedOperator role\nDescription: Use this role if you want to enable users to import selected transport requests in an import queue, but not all requests.  See:   Security  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-26\nValid as Of: 2025-08-26\nVersion: 2508a\n\n--- Record 205 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Behavior Changes of Task Instances REST APIs\nDescription: According to the latest update, APIs for patching and retrieving task contexts are corrected. As a result, task context is now independent of workflow contexts right after input evaluation. The system now ensures this independence, whereas previously it relied solely on modelling best practices.The system processes follow-up actions after completing a task asynchronously. In rare cases, errors from Forms and Approval Forms may now appear on the Logs section of the Instance Details view instead of coming through the API responses. Only users with the Administrator role can see the logs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-26\nValid as Of: 2025-08-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 206 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Download Model for Guided Process Definitions\nDescription: You can now download the latest deployed version of the Guided Process definition. See Processes and Workflows.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-26\nValid as Of: 2025-08-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 207 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Transition Guide - From My Inbox to SAP Task Center\nDescription: A new guide on how to transition from My Inbox to SAP Task Center is available. For more information, see Transition Guide to SAP Task Center.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-26\nValid as Of: 2025-08-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 208 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Deprecation of SAP Ariba Category Management connector\nDescription: Effective August 25, 2025, the SAP Ariba Category Management connector will be deprecated. This change is due to an update of the business solution’s local user store, which no longer requires user provisioning jobs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-12\nValid as Of: 2025-08-25\nVersion: 28165\n\n--- Record 209 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Deprecation of SAP Ariba Category Management connector\nDescription: Effective August 25, 2025, the SAP Ariba Category Management connector will be deprecated. This change is due to an update of the business solution’s local user store, which no longer requires user provisioning jobs.\nA